For each stroke:

1. Intake Stroke: Valves open, intake valve allows air in, exhaust valve closes. Piston moves down, drawing in air-fuel mixture.

2. Compression Stroke: Both valves closed. Piston moves up, compressing the mixture. Pressure rises, temperature increases.

3. Power Stroke: Spark plug ignites the compressed mixture (gasoline) or diesel auto-ignites. High-pressure gases expand, pushing piston down, turning crankshaft via camshaft.

4. Exhaust Stroke: Exhaust valve opens, intake closes. Piston moves up, expelling burned gases out.

